{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27289710","formula":"C₂₁H₂₃NO₃","hill":"C21H23NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":21.0,"H":23.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Proroxan"},"descriptions":{"en":"Proroxan (INN; also known as pyrroxane and pirroksan) is a pharmaceutical drug used as an antihypertensive and in the treatment of Ménière's disease, motion sickness, and allergic dermatitis. Proroxan is a non-selective alpha-blocker (α-adrenoreceptor antagonist). Proroxan was developed in the 1970s at the Institute of Toxicology of the USSR Ministry of Health and today is primarily used in Russia.","ru":"Пророксан (Пирроксан, Pyrroxanum, Prorxan hydrochloride) — лекарственное средство, преимущественно центральный α-адреноблокатор.","uk":"Пророксан (лат. Proroxanum) — синтетичний антигіпертензивний, седативний та протисвербіжний препарат, що належить до групи альфа-адреноблокаторів та є похідним піролідину. Пророксан застосовується як перорально, так і підшкірно та внутрішньом'язово."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":36303,"mass":337.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CN(CC1C2=CC=CC=C2)CCC(=O)C3=CC4=C(C=C3)OCCO4","inchikey":"GZIISXIDAZYOLI-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-(2,3-dihydro-1,4-benzodioxin-6-yl)-3-(3-phenylpyrrolidin-1-yl)propan-1-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"36303","atoms":48,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.444,"y":-2.698,"z":0.23,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.983,"y":2.049,"z":-0.336,"el":"O"},{"x":-7.091,"y":0.161,"z":0.215,"el":"O"},{"x":1.816,"y":-0.121,"z":-0.487,"el":"N"},{"x":4.037,"y":0.558,"z":-0.537,"el":"C"},{"x":3.16,"y":-0.698,"z":-0.532,"el":"C"},{"x":3.282,"y":1.494,"z":0.424,"el":"C"},{"x":1.875,"y":0.913,"z":0.546,"el":"C"},{"x":0.789,"y":-1.117,"z":-0.223,"el":"C"},{"x":5.505,"y":0.382,"z":-0.217,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.601,"y":-0.481,"z":-0.199,"el"